     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><i>Question:    </i></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">Can an R + Shiny + DT, set a column filter dynamically from server side code ?</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><i>Context:       </i></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">My shiny app has two tabPanels each with it&#39;s own DT.  I&#39;ll refer to these as tabPanel#1 (with datatable <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/1\" title=\"support additional capabilities of jslider\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(3,102,214)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792389328614000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2j3wpVe-iXhD_tydqPHHDj\">#1</a>) which contains aggregated data.   tabPanel#2 (with datatable <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/2\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(3,102,214)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792389328614000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Ch9PTSLDgaxvz9-puaiRw\">#2</a>) contains detailed data.  Would like drill down capabilites.  Clikcing on tabPanel#1 will render and display tabPanel #2.  However datatable <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/2\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(3,102,214)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792389328614000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Ch9PTSLDgaxvz9-puaiRw\">#2</a>. will display a subset of it&#39;s data based on a value contained in datatable <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/1\" title=\"support additional capabilities of jslider\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(3,102,214)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792389328614000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2j3wpVe-iXhD_tydqPHHDj\">#1</a> in a specific row/column value.</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">Hopefully I&#39;ve articulated this clearly.</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">I&#39;ve tinkered with code which will filter the data.frame behind datatable#2 however this is not desirable for several reasons. I&#39;d strongly prefer to keep the filtering within the datatable.</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">The closest I&#39;ve found to this capability is here<br style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><a href=\"https://datatables.net/reference/api/column().search()\" style=\"box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(3,102,214)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://datatables.net/reference/api/column().search()&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792389328615000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2mSiOZxj6LOEl-jaelkuuj\">https://datatables.net/reference/api/column().search()</a><br style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">However the language contained in this example is not clear to me, nor is how to implement this in R/Shiny.</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\"><br></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">Thank you in advance!</p></div>"
